    {
      "id": "2eeb086f70843a169c78b445644bdc48050d7af4",
      "short_id": "2eeb086f",
      "created_at": "2022-10-16T21:24:06.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "44a17f395f1c52901f23e54d306614bbda4460bb"
      ],
      "title": "H265: Support RPS prediction in h265 SPS",
      "message": "H265: Support RPS prediction in h265 SPS\n\nAccording to Rec. ITU-T H.265 7.3.7 and 7.4.8,\nwhen there are multiple RPS in SPS,\nRPS can be predicted from previous ones.\n\nBut NumDletaPocs used to be a local variable for each RPS,\nprediction will always fail.\nIn this change, NumDletaPocs is  moved from dissect_h265_st_ref_pic_set\nto dissect_h265_seq_parameter_set_rbsp, to allow access to previous RPS\ndata.\n\nThis change also move each RPS into a subtree.\n\nFix #18481\n",
      "author_name": "Bin Peng",
      "author_email": "binpengsmail@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-10-15T23:06:24.000+08:00",
      "committer_name": "Alexis La Goutte",
      "committer_email": "alexis.lagoutte@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2022-10-16T21:24:06.000+00:00",
